  "verbalization": "Alitretinoin is implicated in the target pathway leading to the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14 through a series of molecular interactions involving a common intermediate compound, 3-[2-[4-[5-[2-(2,3-Dihydroxyphenyl)ethyl]-2-hydroxyphenoxy]phenyl]ethyl]benzene-1,2-diol. This compound is identified as a target of multiple drugs, including alitretinoin, OC-314, and COLO-679, suggesting a shared mechanism of action. The evidence suggests that alitretinoin may act through a common pathway that ultimately targets the proteasome regulatory subunit 14, potentially by modulating the activity of the intermediate compound. The presence of multiple overlapping targets and the shared biochemical profile of the intermediates imply a possible mechanism of action involving the regulation of proteasome function, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
